.SH NAME
ssoosshd-nss-override - List, set or unset this host's per-user overrides.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoosshd-nss override [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Edits the host override file (--overrides) atomically and asks the running daemon to re-read it. An override replaces the server's uid, gid, home or shell for one user on this host only, and never takes a uid or gid outside min_id..max_id.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for override


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--admin-socket\fP="/run/ssoossh-nss/admin.sock"
	the admin socket the CLI and the daemon share

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss.yaml"
	the daemon's configuration file

.PP
\fB--overrides\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss-overrides.yaml"
	the host override file


